stateDiagram-v2
    state "LOAN INSTALLMENT" as LI {
        [*] --> Pending: loan approved, schedule generated
        Pending --> Deducted: period reached & PayrollEntry created\nwith LOAN_DEDUCT component
        Pending --> Skipped: HR manually skips this month\n(e.g. employee on unpaid leave)
        Deducted --> [*]
        Skipped --> [*]
    }

    state "DISBURSEMENT BATCH" as DB {
        [*] --> Pending_DB: POST /disbursements
        Pending_DB --> Generated_DB: CSV/Excel file built & uploaded
        Generated_DB --> Confirmed_DB: finance officer confirms\nbank portal upload
        Confirmed_DB --> PartiallyFailed_DB: one or more records\nmarked Failed
        Confirmed_DB --> Completed_DB: all records Transferred
        PartiallyFailed_DB --> Completed_DB: failed records resolved/reversed
    }

    state "BANK TRANSFER RECORD" as BTR {
        [*] --> Pending_BTR
        Pending_BTR --> Transferred_BTR: bank confirms
        Pending_BTR --> Failed_BTR: bad IBAN / closed account
        Failed_BTR --> Reversed_BTR: funds returned to company
    }

    note right of LI
        LoanInstallment.Status is set the moment
        its PayrollEntry is created — this is what
        updates EmployeeLoan.RemainingAmount (§20.3)
    end note

    note right of BTR
        A transfer's own status is independent of
        PayrollEntry.Status — a bank-side failure
        must NOT reopen an already-Locked payroll
        snapshot (§19.2)
    end note
